 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Hi, my Hotpoint Aquarius dryer is taking forever to dry and the top gets really hot. Model is TCM580GUK if that helps"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "From what you have described, the most likely cause is clean the lint filter and the condenser/heat exchanger. Can you tell me whether filters/condenser not cleaned recently?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Honestly, no, I don't clean them as often as I should. The door filter has a thick layer of fluff on it, and I sometimes forget to clean it. The condenser at the front bottom had lint packed on the fins, and I've rinsed it and it looks cleaner now. The top of the dryer also feels very hot to the touch, and I often run it while I'm out at work."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "From what you have described, the most likely cause is clean the lint/fluff filter. When did you last clean the lint filter and (on a condenser/heat-pump) the condenser?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "I'm afraid I can't say exactly when I last cleaned the door filter, it's been a while. I only rinsed the condenser just now, so before that I can't remember when it was last done."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "From what you have checked, this needs an appliance engineer to look at it: the next steps are beyond the checks that are safe to do yourself."
  }
 ],
